{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I send an angel before you</b> — Here they were informed that they were destined to sin, and the Shekhinah says, \"For I will not go up in your midst\" (Exodus 33:3). <b>For My name is in him</b> is connected to the beginning of the verse: take heed of him, for My name is associated within him. And our Sages interpreted (Sanhedrin 38b) that this is Metatron, whose name is like the name of his Master — Metatron in gematria equals Shaddai. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 23:21). And in Exodus Rabbah (Exodus Rabbah 32:8) I also saw that there are those who interpret this as referring to the matter of the calf.\n\nAnd one may ask, for behold that decree was not fulfilled, since the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, \"And I will send an angel before you, for I will not go up in your midst\" (Exodus 33:2–3), and Moses sought mercy concerning it and said, \"If Your presence does not go, do not bring us up from here, and how then shall it be known that I have found favor in Your eyes, I and Your people — is it not by Your going with us?\" (Exodus 33:15–16), and the Holy One, blessed be He, was appeased by him and said, \"Even this thing that you have spoken I will do\" (Exodus 33:17). And thus they said (Sanhedrin ibid.), even as an escort they did not accept him, as it is written, \"If Your presence does not go, do not bring us up from here.\"\n\nAnd the answer according to this opinion is that that decree was not fulfilled with Moses in his lifetime — this is what he said (Exodus 33:16), \"And I and Your people shall be distinguished,\" and He said (Exodus 33:17), \"For you have found favor in My eyes, and I have known you by name,\" and further He said (Exodus 34:10), \"And all the people among whom you are shall see.\" But after the death of Moses our master, He sent them an angel — and this is what Scripture says (Joshua 5:13–14): \"And it was, when Joshua was in Jericho, that he lifted his eyes and saw, and behold, a man stood opposite him with his sword drawn in his hand. And he said to him, Are you for us or for our adversaries? And he said, No, for I am the prince of the host of YHWH; now I have come.\" And there you will see that Joshua asked him, \"What does my master say to his servant?\" (Joshua 5:14), and he did not command him anything that was revealed to him on his account, but only said to him, \"Remove your sandals from your feet\" (Joshua 5:15), and did not clarify why he had come. Rather, the vision was to inform him that from now on an angel would be dispatched before them for the army when they went out to war. And this is what he said: \"Now I have come\" (Joshua 5:14). And thus they said in Tanhuma (18): \"I am the one who came in the days of Moses your master, and he pushed me away and did not want me to go with him.\" And it is explicitly stated (Exodus Rabbah 32:3): He cancelled the decree that a prince not be given over to them all the days of Moses, and once Moses died, that prince returned to his place — for Joshua sees him, as it is said, \"And it was, when Joshua was in Jericho… and he said, No, for I am the prince of the host of YHWH; now I have come.\" Therefore it is stated, \"Behold, I send an angel.\"\n\nAnd by way of truth, this angel that is promised here is the Angel the Redeemer (Genesis 48:16), in whom the great Name dwells, for ביה YHWH is the Rock of worlds (Isaiah 26:4), and this is what He said, \"I am the El of Beth-el\" (Genesis 31:13), for it is the way of a king to dwell in his house, and Scripture calls him an angel because all the governance of this world is through that quality. And our Sages said (Sanhedrin 38b) that he is Metatron, which is a name for the guide of the way. I have already explained this in the portion of Bo (Ramban on Exodus 12:12). And this is the meaning of <b>to guard you on the way and to bring you to the place that I have prepared</b> — that is, the Temple, as it is written, \"The sanctuary of YHWH, Your hands have established\" (Exodus 15:17). And the meaning of \"which I have prepared\" is: for Myself, to be My holy house and My glory, for there is the complete Throne. And further on I shall mention (Ramban on Exodus 24:1) their intent in \"whose name is like his Master's.\" And behold, his voice is the voice of the living Elohim, and the commandment is to heed his voice from the mouth of the prophets — or the meaning is that they should not cut down the plantings and abandon the Oral Torah, as in the interpretation they gave (Lamentations Rabbah, Proem 2): \"And they spurned the word of the Holy One of Israel\" (Isaiah 5:24) — this is the Oral Torah. And behold, the meaning of \"and hearken to his voice\" (Exodus 23:21) is: to My words, and thus He said, \"For if you diligently hearken to his voice and do all that I speak\" (Exodus 23:22). And Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 23:20) alluded to this, for he translated ארי בשמי מימרה — \"for in My name is His Memra\" — for through him He speaks.\n\nAnd He said, <b>And I will be an enemy to your enemies</b> — that even with the attribute of mercy I will be an enemy to them; <b>and I will oppress your oppressors</b> — through him, with the attribute of judgment. Therefore He explained, <b>For My angel will go before you and bring you to the Amorite</b>, etc., <b>and the Canaanite, and I will destroy them</b> — when He brings you to them, to inform you that He is the one who destroys them. And He mentioned them in singular language, for as one man He will destroy them all. And behold, when this angel dwells within Israel, the Holy One, blessed be He, does not say, \"I will not go up in your midst\" (Exodus 33:3), for My name is within him and he is within Israel. But when they sinned with the calf, He wished to remove His Shekhinah from among them and that an angel, one of His emissaries, would go before them — and Moses sought mercy and He returned and caused His Shekhinah to dwell among them, and there I shall explain the verses, with God's help.\n\nAnd also there in Midrash Rabbah (Exodus Rabbah 32:8) they alluded to this: they said, \"Behold, I send an angel\" — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: He who guarded the fathers will guard the children. And thus you find with Abraham, when he blessed Isaac he said, \"He will send His angel before you\" (Genesis 24:7); with Jacob, \"The angel who redeems me\" (Genesis 48:16) — he said to them, He redeemed me from the hand of Esau, He saved me from the hand of Laban, He fed me and sustained me during the two famines. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: So too now, He who guarded the fathers will guard the children, as it is said, <b>Behold, I send an angel before you</b>. And they further said there (Exodus Rabbah 32:4) explicitly: The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel, Take heed of this emissary, for he does not turn back from his mission — he is the attribute of judgment; do not exchange him, and so forth. In any case, according to all opinions, the midrash that I cited is true: all the days of Moses there was no angelic prince of the host going with them, for Moses filled his place, as it is said (Exodus 17:11), \"And it was, when Moses raised his hand, that Israel prevailed.\" And in the days of Joshua it became necessary for the angel, the prince of the host of YHWH, to come to him to fight their wars — and this is Gabriel, who wages battle on their behalf. And this is why he saw him with his sword drawn in his hand (Joshua 5:13), for he came to execute vengeance among the nations, rebukes among the peoples."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The abbreviation וכו' (\"and so forth\") in the quotation from Exodus Rabbah 32:4 is rendered literally; the midrashic passage continues beyond what Ramban quotes."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:24.407530244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}